WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.774
Cozlin stared at the huge door.

2
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:08.927
"Did you ring the doorbell to see if anyone's home?"

3
00:00:08.928 --> 00:00:12.582
Detective Smith groaned.

4
00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:17.279
Roxy chuckled. "I made the same joke."

5
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:23.762
Cozlin laughed and then pushed on the door. "Grr!"

6
00:00:23.763 --> 00:00:26.217
"That won't work," Roxy said.

7
00:00:26.218 --> 00:00:31.076
"Even I can't open it."

8
00:00:31.077 --> 00:00:32.495
Cozlin shrugged.

9
00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:37.579
"It was worth a try. Let's see if I can move through it."

10
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.345
She took a deep breath and stepped into the door.

11
00:00:41.346 --> 00:00:44.226
Zimp! She was on the other side!

12
00:00:44.227 --> 00:00:46.570
The air felt chilly.

13
00:00:46.571 --> 00:00:49.184
"Hey, Rocket Girl!" she shouted.

14
00:00:49.185 --> 00:00:53.513
Her watch beeped, and she opened it.

15
00:00:53.514 --> 00:00:56.233
"Be quiet!" Roxy whispered.

16
00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:59.997
"Something's in there, and we don't want to wake it up again!"

17
00:00:59.998 --> 00:01:06.053
"Oops," Cozlin whispered. "Sorry!"

18
00:01:06.054 --> 00:01:11.793
She flew down the long, dark tunnel, which opened into a large chamber.

19
00:01:11.794 --> 00:01:13.678
The air felt warmer.

20
00:01:13.679 --> 00:01:18.113
Torches lit the chamber, and piles of shiny gold lay everywhere.

21
00:01:18.114 --> 00:01:22.205
Cozlin gasped. "I never saw so much—"

22
00:01:22.206 --> 00:01:24.560
Snort!

23
00:01:24.561 --> 00:01:26.887
Cozlin dropped flat to the ground.

24
00:01:26.888 --> 00:01:28.281
She wasn't alone.

25
00:01:28.282 --> 00:01:30.319
She peered through the darkness.

26
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.700
Something was on the other side of the chamber.

27
00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:39.365
She grabbed a torch and moved closer.

28
00:01:39.366 --> 00:01:41.971
In the torchlight Cozlin saw a tail.

29
00:01:41.972 --> 00:01:45.480
Her eyes followed the tail to a large, scaly body.

30
00:01:45.481 --> 00:01:51.238
Wings lay folded along its back, and sharp claws grew from its feet.

31
00:01:51.239 --> 00:01:54.502
"It's a dragon!" Cozlin thought.

32
00:01:54.503 --> 00:01:56.189
The dragon snorted again.

33
00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.791
It turned its head toward her.

34
00:01:58.792 --> 00:02:00.439
Cozlin held her breath.

35
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.249
Then she let out a sigh of relief.

36
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.516
The beast's eyes were closed—it was asleep!

37
00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:11.503
She felt a blast of hot air as the dragon snored peacefully.

38
00:02:11.504 --> 00:02:15.228
"Why is this dragon down here?" she thought.

39
00:02:15.229 --> 00:02:18.536
"And why is all this gold down here?" Suddenly

40
00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:23.102
the dragon's tail twitched and sent gold coins flying. Cozlin

41
00:02:23.103 --> 00:02:28.192
panicked and flew as fast as she could. Zimp!

42
00:02:28.193 --> 00:02:31.339
She popped back through the door. "Well?"

43
00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.279
Roxy said. "What's down there?" Detective

44
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.716
Smith took out his notepad. "Lots

45
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:40.156
of gold!" Cozlin said. "Huh,"

46
00:02:40.157 --> 00:02:42.054
Roxy said. "But

47
00:02:42.055 --> 00:02:45.567
what about the sound the construction workers heard?" "Oh,

48
00:02:45.568 --> 00:02:48.682
yeah." Cozlin scratched the back of her neck. "That

49
00:02:48.683 --> 00:02:51.496
was probably the dragon." Detective

50
00:02:51.497 --> 00:02:55.259
Smith dropped his notepad. "The what?" "But

51
00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.040
don't worry," Cozlin said quickly. "It's

52
00:02:58.041 --> 00:03:02.252
fast asleep. It won't even know we're taking the gold." "Whoa!

53
00:03:02.253 --> 00:03:05.451
Hold on," Roxy said. "That

54
00:03:05.452 --> 00:03:09.059
sounds dangerous—and it's stealing." "That

55
00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.963
gold obviously doesn't belong to anyone," Cozlin said. "And

56
00:03:13.964 --> 00:03:16.899
gold is really valuable on Delkor. We

57
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.919
could do good things with it." Detective

58
00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.452
Smith nodded. "Nobody

59
00:03:20.453 --> 00:03:23.300
is going to claim that gold. And

60
00:03:23.301 --> 00:03:26.951
the police department needs new cars—and printers. Mine

61
00:03:26.952 --> 00:03:29.456
keeps getting jammed." Roxy

62
00:03:29.457 --> 00:03:32.832
frowned. "I'm surprised at you two. We're

63
00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:36.380
not touching that gold till we find out more about it. And

64
00:03:36.381 --> 00:03:40.217
right now that dragon isn't bothering anyone. Let's

65
00:03:40.218 --> 00:03:44.681
keep it that way!" ***

66
00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:47.591
Cozlin was back on Delkor.

67
00:03:47.592 --> 00:03:51.360
She was in the palace, telling King Radnik about her discovery.

68
00:03:51.361 --> 00:03:55.587
His face lit up. "That's amazing, Kid Comet.

69
00:03:55.588 --> 00:03:59.617
We could build new schools and hospitals with that gold!"

70
00:03:59.618 --> 00:04:02.367
"I know," she said.

71
00:04:02.368 --> 00:04:04.539
The king paced back and forth.

72
00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.694
"And you're sure the Earthlings don't want it?"

73
00:04:08.695 --> 00:04:11.557
"Uh, yeah," Cozlin said.

74
00:04:11.558 --> 00:04:14.366
"I guess gold isn't valuable there."

75
00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:16.458
The king stopped pacing.

76
00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:19.765
"Well, gold is very valuable here.

77
00:04:19.766 --> 00:04:24.961
I'll have a portal prepared immediately."

